      "factual_description": "Wolf Trap presents violinist Daniel Hope and pianist Maxim Lando at The Barns on Sunday, November 1, 2026 at 3:00 PM in The Gilded Age: Part I, the opening recital of a two-part series curated by Hope. The program is Enescu's Impromptu Concertante; Ravel's Violin Sonata No. 1 and the Blues movement from Violin Sonata No. 2; Elgar's Salut d'Amour and Chanson de Nuit; and Franck's Violin Sonata in A major. Wolf Trap frames the recital around the meeting of European musical refinement and American reinvention around the turn of the 20th century, with Hope and Lando providing moderated context during the performance.",
